    <string name="legal_no_browser">No browser is available to open this page.</string>
    <string name="legal_privacy_body">Peering does not collect analytics.\n\nKept on this phone: the keys that identify this phone to your computers, the list of computers you have paired, and the relay time used each day.\n\nSent between this phone and your computer: the picture, your keyboard and pointer input, and the files and agent chats you open. The connection is encrypted end to end. When a session goes through the relay, the relay forwards only that ciphertext and cannot read the screen, the input or the files.\n\nThe camera is used only to read the pairing code on your computer. Local network access is used to find your computers.</string>
    <string name="legal_terms_body">Peering lets you see and control a computer that you own or are allowed to operate. Use it only on computers you are authorised to control.\n\nRelay time: a relayed session is free for 30 minutes per day. Paid access removes the daily limit. Purchases are handled by Google Play and follow its refund rules.\n\nThe app is provided as it is, without warranty. The complete terms are on the web page.</string>
    <string name="legal_open_source_body">Peering is built with open source software under the Apache License 2.0:\n\nKotlin and kotlinx (coroutines, serialization)\nJetpack Compose and AndroidX\nMaterial 3 for Compose\nOkHttp\nZXing\nCameraX\nGoogle Play Billing Library</string>
