    <string name="tour_install_title">Install it once</string>
    <string name="tour_install_body">Put Peering on the computer you want to reach and open it. That is the whole setup: no account, router changes, or settings to configure.</string>
    <string name="tour_pair_title">Pair once. Stay connected.</string>
    <string name="tour_pair_body">Choose your computer, compare the six-digit code, and Peering remembers it. Next time, reconnect nearby or from another network without pairing again.</string>
    <string name="tour_sources_title">See exactly what you need</string>
    <string name="tour_sources_body">Bring over a whole display, one app, a single window, or any of your Spaces. Jump between them whenever you like without ending the session.</string>
    <string name="tour_controls_title">Your computer, under your fingers</string>
    <string name="tour_controls_body">Tap, type, scroll, zoom, use shortcuts, or steer the pointer with the joystick. Switch to Observe whenever you only want to look.</string>
    <string name="tour_follows_title">Your session follows you</string>
    <string name="tour_follows_body">Leave the app or lock your phone without losing the connection. Picture in Picture keeps your computer in view, while a notification keeps the session close at hand.</string>
    <string name="tour_mosaic_title">See everything at once</string>
    <string name="tour_mosaic_body">Lay out windows, apps and displays side by side and watch them all live. Tap any tile to take control, and come back to the arrangement when you are done.</string>
    <string name="tour_notifications_title">Told when a shell is waiting</string>
    <string name="tour_notifications_body">A build that finishes, a prompt for a password, a command that wants an answer: the computer tells you, on the lock screen and with the app closed.</string>
    <string name="tour_plans_title">Start free. Go farther when you need.</string>
    <string name="tour_plans_body">Use Peering on your own network for free, for as long as you like. Upgrade when you want more relay time or the tools built for working away from your computer.</string>
